<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taif</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ta'if</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taif is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> mountains of western Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, at an altitude of about 1,800 metres. In the time of Muhammad it was the home of the Thaqif tribe and resisted a Muslim siege in 630 before submitting. Known for its fruit and cooler climate, it later served as a summer seat of the Sharifs of Mecca and was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a>'s forces in 1924.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taif.jpg" alt="Taif" width="320" height="136" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: عباد ديرانية · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B7%D8%A7%D8%A6%D9%81_%D9%85%D9%86_%D8%AC%D8%A8%D9%84_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%87%D8%AF%D9%891.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
